  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Sasanquasaponin I may interact with HepG2 through multiple pathways. The compound is associated with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a target of both Sasanquasaponin I and Jerantinine B, and these targets are ultimately linked to HepG2. Additionally, Sasanquasaponin I is also linked to 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is targeted by a compound similar to the one involved in the interaction with Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This indicates that Sasanquasaponin I may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms, potentially targeting distinct components of cellular processes in HepG2 cells. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a possible role for Sasanquasaponin I in modulating cellular functions in HepG2, though the exact mechanism and extent of its interaction remain to be fully elucidated.",
